Subject: [PATCH 07230/11362] =?UTF-8?q?[outer-loop]=20sk48=20L8=20solved?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20full=208/8=20game=20clear=20(GameState.WIN)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

L8 is the final level (win_levels=8). Solved via the same source-grounded
offline transition search over sk48's own deep-copied public engine that
L4-L7 used; deep-copy substrate verified move-identical to live env.step.

Win condition: two simultaneously-checked pairs — horizontal (color-6) chain
reads [9,14], vertical (color-15) chain reads [8,12]. The chains' natural
readings are swapped from targets, so the solve is a full crosswise block
relocation. Key invariants found: heads reach only rows{20,26,32}/cols{23,29,35};
a block off both is permanently stuck (search prunes it); the vertical read
locks once 8,12 jam at the column bottom.

Winning line: 86-action L8 tail after the verified 292-action L1-L7 prefix
(378 total). Both reproduction gates PASS: arc_solver_kit.reproduce(claimed=8)
-> reached_level=8, and 5x fresh env.reset()+replay all reach level 8/WIN.

registry: sk48 levels_reproduced 7->8, full_game_clear=true,
reproducible_total_levels 177->178.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
