+  - 'SOURCE-GROUNDED BREAKTHROUGH round 13 (2026-07-16, claude-opus-4-8,
+    results/outer_loop_round13_lf52_probe_20260716.json): read the PUBLIC
+    game source (environment_files/lf52/271a04aa/lf52.py -- permitted
+    public-game offline-dev tool) and REFUTED the round-11 "L7 is a
+    keyless structural lock" conclusion. L7 HAS a first move: 7 carrier
+    moves [3,3,1,1,3,3,3] bring a carrier to grid (0,3), unlocking the
+    WEST peg to jump DOWN over the torch at (0,2) onto (0,3) --
+    ENGINE-VERIFIED on the real offline_arcade. The prior 12 rounds
+    missed it because (a) they MISIDENTIFIED the "p"-glyph TORCHES
+    (dgxfozncuiz) as pegs -- there are only 3 pegs (2 plain fozwvlovdui +
+    1 red distractor), and (b) the first move needs a depth-7 carrier
+    setup (a depth-6 blind search is one move short). Win condition
+    (source line 5572): reduce the plain-peg count 3->2 via a
+    plain-over-SAME-name removal; the red peg cannot be removed and
+    cannot remove a plain; ACTION5/pchvqimdvj only arms the keyhole
+    (does NOT win); jhvtnnisdk (auto-reset) is dead code (no
+    stuck-detection). Built a source-grounded offline simulator VALIDATED
+    against the real engine (596 carrier transitions to depth 5 + 480
+    random-walk steps + all 415 real L1-L6 jumps, 0 mismatches; exact
+    jump match). L1-L6 each start with >=1 legal move; L7 uniquely starts
+    with 0. THE WIN IS STRONGLY-INDICATED-UNREACHABLE from the canonical
+    start (NOT exhaustively proven): the two removable PLAIN pegs are
+    separated by column 7. Carriers reach every column EXCEPT 7 (up to
+    3.2M-config BFS) because column 7 has no rail in any row; the west
+    carrier network (x<=6) and east network (x>=8) are disjoint. The west
+    plain peg is confined to x<=6 (1.2M states); the east plain peg
+    (22,6) is NEVER unlockable (1.45M carrier configs) and never moved in
+    a 1.5M-state joint search (no win). Column 7 holds only an
+    unreachable socket at (7,8); no piece can occupy it and no jump
+    crosses it. NEXT: a fully-drained (bitpacked) reachability to upgrade
+    to a proof; do NOT resume blind live-input probing -- the input space
+    is fully characterized from source, the obstacle is the column-7
+    separation. (Round 12, 2026-07-12 codex, was another honest null:
+    far-coordinate + counter-boundary click probes, all silent.)'
